  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peace Please!</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project promotes peace, freedom of religion and belief (FORB), and social cohesion in the Far North Cameroon, focusing on the sub-divisions, Mora, Kolofata, and Tokombere, areas impacted by religious tensions and Boko Haram. It empowers religious leaders, traditional chiefs, and local communities to advocate for FoRB and resolve conflicts through interfaith committees, community activities, and shared spaces. By building the capacity of local committees and platforms, the project fosters tolerance and cooperation between Christians, Muslims, and traditional groups. Expanding into new areas, the project ensures sustainability through local ownership, long-term training, and legal recognition of village committees, aiming to prevent radicalization and build a peaceful future free from FORB violations</narrative>
  </description>
